    "display_name": "Static Constants",
    "long_instructions": "## Create an App Shell\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n**Goal**: Store the app's title and date in a local appConfig object and display them instantly. This creates a fast app shell so the user isn't staring at a blank screen while waiting for the internet.\r\n\r\n\r\n**Do This:**\r\n\r\n\r\n1. Create a `const` object named `appConfig`. Inside, add a `title` (text) and a `date` (text).\r\n2. Write a function named `renderAppShell`. Inside, update the display to use the title and date from your `appConfig` object.\r\n3. Call `renderAppShell()` at the bottom of your code so the text appears on the screen immediately.",
